oms 1
// Gate 6 (spec §12), Kamidori: record 0 of a generated append catalog (selector 4; the install mounts 1..3).
// Native op 0x143 runs it at INIT2, during boot. It leaves a message in a string cell no shipped script uses; the
// edited SC0000 shows it.
script "$4$OMSAUTO.BIN"
use kamidori.globals

    GS[0x9000] = set_string("[OMS] The append catalog's autorun script ran at boot.")

    // It also edits an existing unit, 緑プテテット (EBINIT unit 761), which spawns in the first stage
    // (一陣の訓練地). The table cells sit above the saved bank prefix, so boot rebuilds them and the edit holds
    // after a load (docs/kamidori-data-tables.md, "Unit definitions").
    // The registry's unit table names the fields (spec §5.3). With a constant record each field is its cell
    // (§7.6), so the block compiles to three movs: G[0x2c1524], G[0x2c9285] and G[0x2cb9c1].
    with unit[761] {
        .stats.max_hp = 150           // 12 → 150
        .experience_reward = 999      // 10 → 999
        .drop_chance.drop_1 = 100     // drop 1 (緑の液): 30% → 100%
    }
    exit
